<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouse.xml   UtinniPatches — SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S4

  PLACEHOLDER PawnKindDef for RUT_Placeholder_SumpMouseRace (ThingDefs_Races/,
  this same pass) — see that file's own header for why a new child ThingDef
  rather than patching vanilla Squirrel directly. ParentName="AnimalKindBase"
  and combatPower/ecoSystemWeight match Squirrel's own real PawnKindDef
  values exactly (read via mcp__rimsage__get_def_details) — this stub should
  behave like an ordinary small critter in every respect this pass does not
  deliberately change.

  lifeStages: three entries matching Squirrel's own life-stage count and
  drawSize progression, reusing its real texPath
  (Things/Pawn/Animal/Squirrel/Squirrel — confirmed real, already-loaded)
  with a near-black recolor — the "recolored placeholder" the kit spec's
  own S4 text calls for. No new art, no DEPLOY_HOLD needed.

  NOT added to RUT_Sump's own wildAnimals list and not wired into any
  GenStep — this pass's own scope is proving the wander-validator and
  filth-deposit mechanism compiles and is reachable, not populating the
  Sump biome with live wildlife (that is roster-pass content authoring,
  same "compiles now, first live spawn later" posture this item's own S1/S2
  spike pass already used for RM_CompFloodIgniter/RM_CompWorkedLottery).
-->
<Defs>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
